1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,760
小林是一位听障人士，正在独自出行。
Xiaolin is deaf or hard of hearing and is travelling independently.

2
00:00:03,847 --> 00:00:07,957
SoundBridge，把重要的环境声音，转化为腕上的提醒。
SoundBridge turns important environmental sounds into cues on her wrist.

3
00:00:08,044 --> 00:00:11,420
这一次，我们跟随她走过一段日常道路。
Follow her along an everyday journey.

4
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,533
骑行者从左后方接近，车铃响起。
A cyclist approaches from behind on the left and rings a bell.

5
00:00:15,632 --> 00:00:20,420
四个麦克风接收声音，识别车铃后，发出三次短振。
Four microphones capture the sound. Recognizing the bicycle bell triggers three short pulses.

6
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:25,929
三次短振引起注意，小林抬腕查看类别和来向。
Three short pulses get her attention. Xiaolin checks the sound class and direction on her wrist.

7
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:29,420
她转头确认，靠边让行，等骑行者通过。
She looks around, moves aside and lets the cyclist pass.

8
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:34,318
手表上的四个麦克风，位于不同的位置。
Four microphones sit at different positions on the watch.

9
00:00:35,373 --> 00:00:40,365
比较同一次声音到达的微小时差，可以估算声音的来向。
Tiny differences in arrival time help estimate where the sound came from.

10
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:47,420
骑行者从左后方经过左前方，空间位置与表盘角度同步变化。
As the cyclist moves from rear left to front left, the source position and dial angle change together.

11
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:51,069
来到路口，一辆车从右前方驶来。
At a crossing, a vehicle approaches from the front right.

12
00:00:51,155 --> 00:00:55,935
识别鸣笛后，两次长振提醒她，表盘显示类别和来向。
Recognizing the horn triggers two long pulses. The dial shows the sound class and direction.

13
00:00:56,021 --> 00:00:59,420
收到振动后，她抬腕查看，在路缘内停步观察。
Feeling the vibration, she checks her watch and stops before the curb.

14
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:04,990
看清车辆的行进方向，她留在安全的位置等待。
She checks the vehicle direction and waits in a safe position.

15
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:09,420
等车辆通过，确认道路情况，再继续前行。
After it passes, she checks the road and continues.

16
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:16,467
声音类别告诉她，发生了什么；来向提示帮助她决定往哪里看。
The sound class explains what happened. Direction helps her decide where to look.

17
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:22,073
表盘同时呈现角度、文字和指示标记，减少理解的负担。
Angles, text and a pointer make the cue easier to understand.

18
00:01:22,147 --> 00:01:27,420
触觉引起注意，视觉补充信息，最后由她观察和判断。
Touch gets her attention. Visual cues add context. She observes and decides.

19
00:01:28,550 --> 00:01:32,942
在步道旁停稳后，小林调整手表的提醒方式。
Stopped safely beside the path, Xiaolin adjusts her watch.

20
00:01:33,549 --> 00:01:37,965
振动强度和文字大小，按照她的感受来设置。
She sets vibration strength and text size to suit her.

21
00:01:38,572 --> 00:01:43,420
让每一次提醒清楚而舒适，帮助她从容关注周围。
Clear, comfortable cues help her stay aware of her surroundings.

22
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:48,798
她继续行走时，我们看看手表内部如何协作。
As she continues walking, we look inside the watch.

23
00:01:49,969 --> 00:01:56,881
麦克风收集信号，处理电路识别声音，显示模组和触觉马达传达提醒。
Microphones capture signals. The board identifies sounds. The display and haptic actuator deliver the cue.

24
00:01:58,052 --> 00:02:05,420
部件平稳展开，再沿原位收回。技术的目的，是让重要线索及时被感知。
The layers separate smoothly and return to place. Their purpose is to make important cues perceptible.

25
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:11,542
另一位骑行者从右后方接近，手表再次识别车铃。
Another cyclist approaches from behind on the right. The watch identifies the bell.

26
00:02:11,729 --> 00:02:16,505
短振与右后方提示出现，小林抬腕，转头观察。
Short pulses and a rear-right cue appear. Xiaolin checks her wrist and looks around.

27
00:02:16,692 --> 00:02:21,420
她让出空间，保持对周围的警觉，等待对方通过。
She makes space, stays aware of her surroundings and lets the rider pass.

28
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:26,061
安全感，来自及时的线索，也来自自己的判断。
Confidence comes from timely cues and her own judgment.

29
00:02:26,143 --> 00:02:29,420
SoundBridge，为听障人士设计的环境感知手表。
SoundBridge. An environmental awareness watch for deaf and hard-of-hearing people.
